    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“Have you started "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "raising lobsters"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " yet?” Recently, this strange question has been spreading across China’s tech world. But don’t look for seafood. This is actually about OpenClaw, a powerful AI assistant nicknamed “the lobster” for its bright red logo. From tech "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "geeks",
            "zh": "科技极客"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to giant companies, everyone is trying to master this new AI agent."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "OpenClaw is an "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "open-source",
            "zh": "开源的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " project, which means its code is freely available for everyone. It is so popular that it quickly became the most-starred project on "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "GitHub",
            "zh": "一个开源项目托管平台"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " within just a few months. However, OpenClaw is not as user-friendly as other AI tools. It requires technical skills to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "install",
            "ref": "v-install"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", so a new market has appeared. People are paying experts large sums of money to set up their “lobsters”. Some service providers have even earned up to 260,000 "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "yuan"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in just a few days."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Chinese tech titans are not falling behind. "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Tencent",
            "zh": "腾讯"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "ByteDance",
            "zh": "字节跳动"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " have "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "launched",
            "ref": "v-launch"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " their own versions that are much easier to use, while Xiaomi has also been testing a similar service. Researchers believe OpenClaw will reshape how people work, as AI moves from simply answering questions to planning and completing more complex tasks."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "However, “raising a lobster” comes with risks. Without the right security settings, hackers might steal users’ data. It can also be expensive to run because it consumes a large number of AI "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "tokens",
            "zh": "词元"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Some people believe it is still more of a toy for tech geeks than a tool for everyone. Still, this craze reflects a massive surge of interest in AI across China. The country’s AI industry is growing fast and is expected to exceed 10 "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "trillion",
            "zh": "万亿"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "yuan"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " by 2030."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
